  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nI'm not quite sure how outline is supposed to work with `::picker(select)`. As far as I can tell the `option` element takes up the entire width so the outline will be clipped by the `::picker(select)` box (which has `overflow: auto`). It seems that in Chrome however the `option` element still has 1px wiggle room somehow. It still looks bad as Chrome's outline is 1.5px.\n\nWebKit's macOS outline is much bigger and I'd need to apply a negative `outline-offset` to compensate, but that does not seem ideal.\n\ncc @whatwg/css ",
